# Vector search

This section contains code recipes in various programming languages for solving [vector search](../../concepts/query_execution/vector_search.md) tasks using the {{ ydb-short-name }} SDK.

The operations will be covered in detail:

- [Vector search](#vector-search)

  - [Connecting to {{ ydb-short-name }}](#connect-ydb)
  - [Creating a table](#create-table)
  - [Inserting vectors](#insert-vectors)
  - [Adding an index](#add-vector-index)
  - [Vector search](#search-by-vector)
  - [Final example](#full-example)

This recipe creates a text store with the following structure:

| Field | Explanation |
| --- | --- |
| `id` | text identifier |
| `document` | Text |
| `embedding` | Text vector representation |

The recipe assumes that `embedding` already exists.

## Connecting to {{ ydb-short-name }} {#connect-ydb}

This section describes the minimal required steps to execute queries in {{ ydb-short-name }}.
For more detailed information about connecting to {{ ydb-short-name }}, see the article [{#T}](./init.md).

{% list tabs group=tool %}

- C++


  ```cpp
  #include <ydb-cpp-sdk/client/query/client.h>

  int main() {
      auto driverConfig = NYdb::CreateFromEnvironment(endpoint + "/?database=" + database);
      NYdb::TDriver driver(driverConfig);
      NYdb::NQuery::TQueryClient client(driver);

      // ...
  }
  ```

- Go


  ```go
  package main

  import (
      "context"
      "os"

      "github.com/ydb-platform/ydb-go-sdk/v3"
  )

  func main() {
      ctx, cancel := context.WithCancel(context.Background())
      defer cancel()
      db, err := ydb.Open(ctx,
          os.Getenv("YDB_CONNECTION_STRING"),
      )
      if err != nil {
          panic(err)
      }
      defer db.Close(ctx)
  }
  ```

- Java

  To execute YQL queries, use `QueryClient` — the YQL Query Service client. Retries on transient errors are provided by `SessionRetryContext`, which is built on top of `QueryClient`. For more details on configuring transport and clients, see the article [Driver initialization](./init.md).

  Below is a minimal runnable example: connection, creating `SessionRetryContext`, and checking the connection with the `SELECT 1` query. The `retryCtx` object will be needed in the subsequent steps of the recipe.


  ```java
  import tech.ydb.common.transaction.TxMode;
  import tech.ydb.core.grpc.GrpcTransport;
  import tech.ydb.query.QueryClient;
  import tech.ydb.query.tools.QueryReader;
  import tech.ydb.query.tools.SessionRetryContext;
  import tech.ydb.table.query.Params;

  public class VectorSearchConnectExample {

      public static void main(String[] args) {
          String connectionString = System.getenv().getOrDefault(
                  "YDB_CONNECTION_STRING", "grpc://localhost:2136/local");

          try (GrpcTransport transport = GrpcTransport.forConnectionString(connectionString).build();
               QueryClient queryClient = QueryClient.newClient(transport).build()) {

              // SessionRetryContext automatically retries the query on temporary failures.
              SessionRetryContext retryCtx = SessionRetryContext.create(queryClient).build();

              // Connection check — the same retryCtx is used in the following steps.
              retryCtx.supplyResult(session -> QueryReader.readFrom(
                      session.createQuery("SELECT 1", TxMode.NONE, Params.empty())
              )).join().getValue();
          }
      }
  }
  ```

