## Vector search {#search-by-vector}

To search documents by vector, a special YQL query is used, in which you must define a similarity or distance function.
Available values:

* `CosineSimilarity`
* `InnerProductSimilarity`
* `CosineDistance`
* `ManhattanDistance`
* `EuclideanDistance`

The functions are described in more detail in the documentation on [distance and similarity functions](../../yql/reference/udf/list/knn.md#fuctions-distance).

The method allows you to specify the index name. If it is set, the expression `VIEW index_name` will be added to the query, enabling the use of a vector index during search.

The method returns a list of dictionaries with fields `id`, `document`, and `score` — a number reflecting the similarity (or distance) to the query vector.

